# The CPU power policy follows the AC adapter: unplugging drops EPP to power
# and the platform profile to quiet, plugging in returns balance_power and
# balanced (power-profile-ac.service has the writes). This used to be a rule
# in the shell (SysState.qml, syncProfile) talking to power-profiles-daemon,
# which meant a stale UPower reading in a QML binding could -- and did -- hold
# the daemon on balanced for whole battery sessions and undo every manual pick
# of power-saver within a minute (docs/2026-09-10-powertop.md). udev sees the
# same ACPI event the kernel does, is coldplugged at boot, and keeps working
# when the shell is confused or not running. The daemon is gone since
# 2026-09-17; the service writes sysfs directly.
#
# RUN+= rather than ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}: a change event on a device unit that is
# already active does not reliably re-start its Wants=, and the adapter is a
# change event every time.
ACTION=="change", SUBSYSTEM=="power_supply", KERNEL=="AC0", RUN+="/usr/bin/systemctl --no-block start power-profile-ac.service"
